LineageOS with backported Security Patches + MicroG support
===========

Getting started
---------------

To get started with Android/LineageOS, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the LineageOS trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/LineageOS-R-ASB/manifest.git -b lineage-18.1-microg --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync -j$(nproc)
```
Btw, if you already have 18.1 synced, you don't have to delete it and fully resync this one. Just run the init command on top of your 18.1 buildsystem and it'll automatically fetch the modified repositories :)  

Security Patches
----------------

The backports are taken from [LineageOS Review](https://review.lineageos.org/q/branch:lineage-18.1) (R_asb_20XX_XX tags)  
See [build repository](https://github.com/LineageOS-R-ASB/build) to check what security patch is merged.  
